# No In-Code Comments

Do not add comments in source code (including `//`, `/* */`, `///`, `#`, or WGSL/GLSL comment forms).

## Why

- Comments increase liability and go stale
- Comments encourage justifying bad patch fixes instead of fixing design
- Readable architecture and naming should make intent obvious

## Required

- Express intent with clear names, small modules, and straightforward control flow
- If something seems to need a comment, refactor until it does not
- Delete existing comments when touching a file

## Forbidden

- Inline, block, or doc comments in application/source files
- Commenting out dead code (delete it)
- "TODO" / "HACK" / "NOTE" comments as substitutes for structure

Exception: license headers required by third-party terms, and comments inside generated files you must not edit.
